# Duskwood and Redridge, second half (about 27 to 29).
#
# Since 2026-11-07 Duskwood and Redridge are played together, so Redridge
# comes at 23+ where its quests fit (Ashenvale and Stonetalon first): Duskwood's first
# loop and Redridge (04-redridge-mountains, with Redridge's elites and Fangore
# at about 25 on the same loop through the Blackrock camps and Galardell
# Valley), then Duskwood's second loop here. The first loop's Darkshire
# visit and its quests are in 04-redridge-mountains.
#
# Flow: fly from Lakeshire to Darkshire -> Blind Mary, the Tranquil Gardens
# Cemetery (the Insane Ghoul), Viktori, Madame Eva -> west: Abercrombie, the
# Raven Hill Cemetery's Skeletal Fiends and Horrors (The Night Watch), Sven ->
# Darkshire (The Night Watch handed in, its third part taken) -> the Skeletal
# Horrors south-east of town (Rot Blossoms) -> Darkshire -> west: Abercrombie,
# the ghouls and Plague Spreaders, Jitters, Sven (Proving Your Worth from 28)
# -> north through Elwynn for training (Shamans in Ironforge by the Deeprun
# Tram, Rogues in Stormwind; Bishop Farthing in the Cathedral) -> the Stormwind
# gryphon to Menethil Harbor, where the next guide (06-wetlands) starts. The
# Night Watch's third part (58) is handed in on the Duskwood return
# (07-thousand-needles), with Look to the Stars' fourth part (181), taken here.
#
# Deviations from the export:
# - Look To The Stars (174): the export finds the Bronze Tube on Venture Co.
#   machines in Stonetalon (a 1-2% drop). The tube comes from the Stormwind
#   Auction House on 04-redridge-mountains' Stormwind stop (Herble Baubbletump,
#   next to Viktori, keeps one and is nearly always sold out, #1348): handed in
#   on the first Darkshire visit, and its second part (175) handed to Blind
#   Mary on her visit; the Insane Ghoul (177, level 26, at the player's level
#   here) is in the Tranquil Gardens' crypt right below her, and Viktori takes
#   the glass on the way into town (fix round 2026-11-20).
# - The Night Watch (57): its Skeletal Fiends and Horrors are worked in the
#   Raven Hill Cemetery on the first west trip and handed to Commander Althea on
#   the Darkshire stop after it (fix round 2026-11-20; it was handed in on the
#   Duskwood return two guides later). Its third part (58, Plague Spreaders
#   27-28) is taken there and worked with Abercrombie's ghoul ribs, which the
#   same ghouls drop.
# - Proving Your Worth (323, Skeletal Raiders 27-28, Healers 26-27, Warders
#   28-29 just east of Sven's camp) is worked on the spot from level 28
#   (`when level>=28`), and Seeking Wisdom (269) goes to Bishop Farthing on the
#   Stormwind walk: his The Doomed Fleet (270) opens Lightforge Iron in Menethil
#   on 06-wetlands. Below 28 it waits for the Duskwood return.
# - Wolves at Our Heels (226) is turned in on the second visit to Sven's camp
#   (Lars stands beside Sven) instead of walking back west for it.
# - Hearthstone: the second loop's Moonbrook footlocker is followed by the
#   hearth back to Darkshire (bound on the first loop's visit,
#   04-redridge-mountains, with the flight path); the walk north through
#   Goldshire (training) to Stormwind's gryphon is on the way to Menethil.
# - No Awaiting Word (236): Watcher Dodds doesn't offer it on Forever (#2148;
#   forever-db/corrections removes it from the data).
# - Redridge's elites (Tharil'zun 19, Gath'Ilzogg 169, Incinerator Gar'im
#   95999, Shadow Magic's Blackrock Shadowcasters 115) and Lieutenant Fangore
#   (180, 26) are on 04-redridge-mountains' loop at about 26-27, where those
#   quests fit: players finished them solo at 21-23 in the recordings, so they
#   are in the route's steps with a tip to group up if you can; the elite
#   Wanted posters' work (169, 95999) is on steps the player opts into
#   (`when group`, #1415: an all-optional step was passed at once, so nobody
#   was led there), Fangore's (not elite) is a plain goal.
# - Worgen in the Woods (173) needs level 23: the step before it says so.
#
# Class quests: Rogues finish Mathias and the Defias with Klaven's Tower
# (2360, 2359, Poisons) at the end: Agent Kearnen and the tower stand just
# over the Westfall border from Raven Hill, and Mathias Shaw is in Stormwind
# on the way to the boat. Optional for Rogues there: The Touch of Zanzil
# (2607-2609, Doc Mixilpixil in the Barracks cellar; Wildflowers and a Leaded
# Vial from Stormwind vendors, a Bronze Tube from the Auction House, the thread
# in the city), 1,305 XP without leaving Stormwind.
# Human Paladins still carrying the Defias Script (1787: 03-loch-modan does Henze Faulk and
# Redemption, 04-redridge-mountains is the fallback) hand it to Gazin Tenorm at the Stormwind
# stop and learn Redemption from Duthorian Rall (1788).
#
# Dusky Crab Cakes (93, taken in 04-redridge-mountains with Jitters' Growling Gut's hand-in): its
# Gooey Spider Legs on the first west trip, handed to Chef Grual on the next Darkshire stop, and
# Return to Jitters (240) handed in on the Raven Hill stop.
# Left out (not in the export): Seasoned Wolf Kabobs (90: Cooking), The Weathered Grave chain
# (225: ends at the elite Mor'Ladim), Ira's Dagger (96137: it starts from a
# drop of the Lost Stalkers, Forever's new Duskwood mobs, at an unknown rate,
# and is not in the new consensus either).
# Refresh (2026): Merrick's Bow (96138) now has a known start, a drop of the
# Lost Watchers; the new consensus does it at 28 with the ogres of Vul'Gol,
# so it is an optional extra in 07-thousand-needles' Duskwood return. The
# Valor Family (98447, a Forever quest listed for Duskwood, level 27)
# is not in our data: no giver, objective or ender we can place, so it is
# not added. The Valor Family 96139 (Sirra Von'Indi) stays as it is.
# The Legend of Stalvan (fix round 2026-11-20): Clerk Daltry's first part (67, taken on 04-redridge-mountains'
# Darkshire stop) is the Old Footlocker in Westfall's Moonbrook, west of Sven's camp at the end of the first west
# trip; Daltry takes it on the Darkshire stop after (68) and sends you to Innkeeper Farley in Goldshire (69, 70),
# then Caretaker Folsom and his Sealed Crate in Stormwind (72), all on the walk north to the gryphon. Its next part
# (74) goes to Marshal Haggard in Elwynn's far east, off the route from here on, so the chain stops there;
# Stalvan Mistmantle himself (98, level 32, not elite in our data) is never reached.
# Checked and skipped: The Missing Diplomat (1274, from Thomas in Stormwind's Trade District, 28) is a chain of
# Stormwind errands (the Keep, the gate, the cheese shop) that then goes to Watcher Backus in Duskwood and on to
# Theramore: after 1243 it is off this route, and the Stormwind part alone is a detour through the Keep for 230 XP a part.

step Fly to Darkshire
  zone Redridge Mountains
  tip Back to the Lakeshire gryphon master: fly to Darkshire for Duskwood's second loop.
  goto 25.5,59.4 "Lakeshire flight master" live
  fly "Darkshire"

step Blind Mary
  zone Duskwood
  tip Her house stands on the hill south-east of Darkshire, above the Tranquil Gardens Cemetery.
  turnin 149                          -- Inside
  accept 154
  turnin 175
  accept 177                              -- Mary's Looking Glass: the Insane Ghoul, in the crypt of the cemetery just below

step Tranquil Gardens Cemetery
  tip The Insane Ghoul (26) hides in the small crypt by the Tranquil Gardens Cemetery, south of Darkshire; the glass is inside.
  collect 1946 quest 177                  -- Mary's Looking Glass; inside
  collect 2794 optional                   -- An Old History Book: a rare drop from Duskwood's mobs
  accept 337 optional

step Viktori Prism'Antras
  tip North into Darkshire: Viktori's house stands at the east end of town, on the way in.
  turnin 177                              -- Viktori Prism'Antras, inside
  accept 181                              -- Look to the Stars: the ogres of Vul'Gol, on your Duskwood return

step Madame Eva
  turnin 154                          -- Inside
  accept 157

